litehtml: include <cstdlib> for atoi() in el_font.cpp

el_font.cpp calls atoi() without including <cstdlib> and relied on
another header to pull it in. libc++ (LLVM 23, CLANG64/CLANGARM64) no
longer does, so the bundled litehtml of Qt Assistant fails to compile:

  el_font.cpp:27:12: error: use of undeclared identifier 'atoi'

Upstream litehtml (master) still lacks the include.

--- a/src/assistant/qlitehtml/src/3rdparty/litehtml/src/el_font.cpp
+++ b/src/assistant/qlitehtml/src/3rdparty/litehtml/src/el_font.cpp
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include "el_font.h"
 #include "document.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 
 
 litehtml::el_font::el_font(const std::shared_ptr<document>& doc) : html_tag(doc)
